  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    Fluxium~ was a mining foreman at ☽'scar Ramtatus~, the Nightshelf colony carved from virgin ice by Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss during Nightfall Shelf's southern expansion. Described as soot-dark and loud, Fluxium~ led crews driving passages through the colony's southern galleries, setting work-chants to old Nightshelf melodies with words rewritten to carry the deep-ice creed: *We keep what we kindle. We owe what we burn.* The crews wore guild-marks — a brazier crossed with a sealed door — and handled fire-cores bare-flippered, though they refused to touch aurora-crystals stored in nearby supply crates. Fluxium~'s team struck what Fissure-Dealer ☽'Sanctteinvaus called the richest fire-core vein yet found in the south gallery.
    
    Fluxium~ later appeared before the Shadow Parliament as a guild-lawyer, serving as defense counsel for the Midnight Claws during their dissolution trial. Wearing mended wrappings, Fluxium~ argued the Claws had sustained fire-core supply to settlements when official channels failed, and called witnesses whose testimony complicated the prosecution's case. The Parliament dissolved the Claws regardless.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771593398474_0", anchor: "the richest fire-core vein yet found in the south gallery", text: "The Rofundis∴rupt collapsed ☽'scar Ramtatus~'s primary vein. The south gallery location makes this almost certainly the same seam. Fluxium~'s crowning professional achievement was locating the deposit whose catastrophic failure would later cripple Nightshelf fire-core exports and destabilize the Flipper Accord's supply assumptions. A forgotten foreman finds the richest vein; the richest vein buries the colony. History does, on occasion, edit itself for effect.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771593398474_1", anchor: "refused to touch aurora-crystals stored in nearby supply crates", text: "Refusal or prohibition? Guild-marks featuring a sealed door suggest the latter. The chant says *We owe what we burn* — debt acknowledged for fire consumed. Aurora-crystals carry no corresponding debt framework in Nightshelf practice. You cannot owe what you will not touch. Neat theology.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771593398474_2", anchor: "the Claws had sustained fire-core supply to settlements when official channels failed", text: "The argument was factually correct. That it failed anyway is the most Nightshelf outcome imaginable — a tribunal that knows the defendant kept people alive and dissolves them regardless, because the question was never whether the Claws were useful but whether they were *authorized.* Fluxium~ came from a tunnel where you handle fire-cores bare-flippered because the work demands it. The Shadow Parliament comes from a chamber where you handle precedent with gloves on because the institution demands it. Two fluencies. One room.", type: :commentary, display: :full
